
== S1  K_c is not IE1
PASS N1  [witness] R = [[0,0,-1],[0,-1,0],[-1,0,0]] is a rotation (R^T R = I, det R = 1)
PASS N2  [witness] actC R phiW = G, the table of c1 (c1 K5: pauliW G = psi psi^T)
PASS N3  [witness] ipW E0 G = -1 (E0 in dualW K_c by c1 K1-K3 and note K.W): G is not in K_c, while phiW is (c1 K6)
PASS N3c  [countercontrol] countercontrol: G lies in Q3 (pauliW G has eigenvalues 1, 0, 0, 0): the same rotation keeps phiW inside Q3, so the failure is a property of K_c -- eigenvalues {1: 1, 0: 3}
NOTE [written] N.R  -- IE1 fails for K_c (phiW in K_c, actC R phiW not in K_c). With cnot gates and identity locals every orientation bit is false, so EvenCycle holds and C fails through IE1 for uniform K_c, for (Q3, Q3, K_c, K_c) and for (K_c, K_c, Q3, Q3).

